# Adlaire-Design Component Contract Matrix

This matrix maps component families to the documents, source files, generated files, JavaScript hooks, samples, and checks that keep each contract synchronized.

`Docs/Master_Spec` remains the higher-level source of truth. This file is a navigation and verification matrix, not a separate implementation authority.

The Generated JavaScript pair contract keeps the listed Deno TypeScript source, generated JavaScript output, generated file header, and documentation coverage synchronized for each behavior surface. The JavaScript public surface contract keeps delegated UI initialization and `window.AdlaireEditor` exposure check-covered. The Sample asset/load contract keeps sample CSS and JavaScript loading aligned with the generated outputs. The CSS target manifest contract keeps `TypeScript/CSS/manifest.ts`, generated CSS outputs, first-line headers, public CSS order, and sample loading synchronized. The Editor runtime module registry contract keeps the flat `TypeScript/Editor/*.ts` file set, `TypeScript/Editor/index.ts`, `Docs/Editor_Master_Spec`, and `EditorUI/editor.js` synchronized. The Deno type-check target coverage keeps the normal TypeScript type-check entrypoints explicit and check-covered.

`Tools/check/adlaire-design-contracts.json` is the JSON check contract manifest for Deno validation targets, the Deno complete validation gate, Generated JavaScript parity contract terms, repositoryInventory, minimum component and interaction contract coverage, Interaction audit contract coverage, and the Visual Baseline hash.

`TypeScript/UI/component-contracts.ts` records representative UI component contracts as TypeScript source metadata. It does not replace this matrix; it gives checks and implementation review a typed source for high-risk synchronized families, generated CSS/JavaScript files, ARIA requirements, state attributes, required icons, sample sections, responsive modes, review surface, review tier, contract owner, contract depth, contract risk, contract lifecycle, platform support, accessibility records, behavior-required contracts, governance records, and required coverage gaps.

`TypeScript/UI/interaction-contracts.ts` records UI interaction contract metadata as TypeScript source metadata. It keeps declarative hooks, shared interaction primitives, source files, generated JavaScript targets, generated parity, event partitions, input modality, optional sample requirements, audit records, state attributes, fallback policies, and state scopes synchronized across public components, forms, content, and WYSIWYG UI.

