- Every contract family has exactly one primary catalog or specification.
- Generated CSS and generated JavaScript stay repository-local outputs.
- Samples confirm representative behavior, but Samples never become the source of truth.
- Accessibility hooks for roles, labels, dismiss controls, focus containment, Escape handling, hidden decorative content, and selected/current state are part of interaction readiness.
- Checks must fail with actionable messages when a source, generated output, catalog, sample, or hook drifts.
- Representative subcontracts define the minimum review granularity for a component family.
- New component families require a matrix row, a catalog or specification owner, and check coverage.
- High-risk synchronized families should be added to `TypeScript/UI/component-contracts.ts` when their catalog, CSS, generated output, JavaScript hook, sample, and check coverage must move together.
